//// C-03 — `std-unsupported-on-target` names the function the program calls,
//// located at the call. `erlang.nodes` is far down `std/erlang`'s `pub
//// declare fn`s; the refusal named `std/erlang.abs`, the module's first, and
//// gave the module rather than the call as its location, sending the reader
//// to a function they did not call. erlang and beam run it: a node that is
//// not distributed knows no other node.

import {erlang} from "std";

pub fn main() {
    @print(erlang.nodes());
}
